WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.330
It's time for Drew's News,

2
00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:04.600
your good news flashlight in the middle of the night.

3
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.510
I personally like a headlamp, hands free.

4
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:09.920
And with me at the desk,

5
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.360
the best co-pilot in the business, Rossy Ross Matthews.

6
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.686
Yes! Hi, everybody!

7
00:00:14.686 --> 00:00:15.519
(audience cheering excitedly)

8
00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:16.352
Hi, hi.

9
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.080
I love you in an olive!

10
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.910
This is the first time I've worn this jacket.

11
00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:23.743
You like?

12
00:00:23.743 --> 00:00:25.240
I love.

13
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.890
I got it at the mall myself,

14
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.070
I did, cute.
(audience laughing warmly)

15
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.980
And the collar on your shirt, very unique.

16
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:32.900
Yeah, I took a risk.

17
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.770
And you, I heard you said

18
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.010
you were doing a Diane Chambers look,

19
00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:37.843
is that what you said?

20
00:00:37.843 --> 00:00:39.970
No, but they were playing "Cheers" backstage.

21
00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:40.803
Oh, they were.

22
00:00:40.803 --> 00:00:43.270
I'm binging "Cheers" on Hulu right now on the train,

23
00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.710
and it's like, some of her looks totally remind me of you.

24
00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.730
You could pull any sort of bloused sleeve-

25
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.370
I love a Diane Chambers reference, I will take it.

26
00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.730
You are welcome for that!

27
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.990
Thank you, Shelley Long!

28
00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.240
And we are sort of the Sam and Diana daytime,

29
00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.142
will we won't we, you know what I mean?

30
00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:02.200
(Ross and Drew laughing amusingly)

31
00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.810
Usually, I'm hawking the idea to you

32
00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:08.410
and you're like, "What are you talking about?"

33
00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.400
I'm like, "Girl, wrong tree you're barking.

34
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.233
Let's move on."
(audience laughing warmly)

35
00:01:11.233 --> 00:01:14.360
I know, it's my life pattern to bark up the wrong tree.

36
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.420
I know you're not interested in me, Rossy.

37
00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.540
I'm interested you in every way, but one.

38
00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.640
And that's why this works.

39
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.190
Exactly. Cheers to you.

40
00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.150
And I am the flower girl at your wedding.

41
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.830
Yes, you are!

42
00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.600
Alright, well before we hit the headlines, we have a PSA

43
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.300
for anyone who's about to take their passport photo.

44
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.133
Yup.

45
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:31.966
How do I know this?

46
00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:34.770
Well, I just tried to upload my new passport photo

47
00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:39.320
and I got a message that said my photo was rejected.

48
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.660
And the reason why was a smile was detected.

49
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.539
Look at her. (Ross laughing amusingly)

50
00:01:44.539 --> 00:01:46.350
I look too happy!

51
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.200
You do!

52
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.458
They rejected my photo!

53
00:01:49.458 --> 00:01:50.530
(Ross laughing amusingly)

54
00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.253
And here is my fully approved passport photo.

55
00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.780
Can you believe this?

56
00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.930
Does anyone know that you are not allowed to smile

57
00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.810
in a passport photo?

58
00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.310
Raise of hands, who knows this?

59
00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.278
Oh, everybody.

60
00:02:06.278 --> 00:02:07.111
(audience laughing amusingly)

61
00:02:07.111 --> 00:02:08.330
Well in your defense,

62
00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:11.160
I only know this 'cause they told me "stop smiling"

63
00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.680
when I got the picture taken.

64
00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.513
Why is this?

65
00:02:13.513 --> 00:02:15.530
Hello, we're literally going into other countries,

66
00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.970
we don't wanna do it smiling?

67
00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.720
Like, I'm friendly, hello!

68
00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.610
But like, what's the difference?

69
00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.610
It's still me.

70
00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.443
Cute!
Me.

71
00:02:27.056 --> 00:02:29.590
(audience laughing amusingly)

72
00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:34.363
Well okay, so everybody now knows no smile!

73
00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.687
Welcome to the country.

74
00:02:36.687 --> 00:02:37.738
(Ross laughing amusingly)

75
00:02:37.738 --> 00:02:40.717
(audience applauding)

76
00:02:40.717 --> 00:02:41.550
Alright, well-

77
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.660
That's hilarious, Drew.

78
00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.690
This story is very meaningful.

79
00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.990
Everyone is tuning into Amy Poehler's

80
00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:51.100
directorial intimate portrait of Lucille Ball

81
00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.760
and Desi Arnaz, called "Lucy and Desi."

82
00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.640
The New York Times reports that the new Amazon documentary

83
00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.710
tells the story of the couple in their own words.

84
00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:02.810
Amy went through hours of audio tapes

85
00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.700 line:15%
to reconstruct their incredible story.

86
00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.770 line:15%
Now, if you've seen the movie that's out,

87
00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:11.060 line:15%
obviously right now, this is a completely different take.

88
00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:11.923 line:15%
Take a look.

89
00:03:13.697 --> 00:03:15.860
"I Love Lucy" built every episode

90
00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:19.840
around that idea of fracture and come back together.

91
00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.970
And I think we crave that as humans.

92
00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.784
No matter what you've done, I forgive you.

93
00:03:25.784 --> 00:03:27.337
(audience laughing relatably)

94
00:03:27.337 --> 00:03:28.960
♪ Will you still love me ♪

95
00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.300
You don't necessarily have to be a funny person

96
00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.502
to get a laugh.

97
00:03:32.502 --> 00:03:33.950
♪ Beautiful ♪

98
00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.591
I'm not a funny person.

99
00:03:35.591 --> 00:03:37.140
♪ Will you still love me? ♪

100
00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.100
The show was one of the most wonderful things

101
00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.040
that happened in my life.

102
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.655
We brought the rafters down.

103
00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.488
(audience laughing)

104
00:03:43.488 --> 00:03:44.568
♪ I know you will ♪

105
00:03:44.568 --> 00:03:46.440
♪ I know you will ♪

106
00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.360
♪ I know that you will ♪

107
00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.853
At the core, it's all about unconditional love.

108
00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.810
(audience cheering happily)

109
00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.023
I know, it's so good.

110
00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.460
Oh my God.

111
00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.440
It's hardcore, but I've been watching it

112
00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.150
